# Trivy CVE exemptions — narrow, per-CVE, with written reason + upgrade plan.
# Each entry MUST include the CVE id, the affected package path, the reason
# the exemption is safe today, and the trigger that retires the exemption.
#
# Adding entries here is a structural escape hatch for the Trivy gate. Use
# sparingly: prefer fixing the dep over ignoring it.
#
# ── Current exemptions ──
#
# CVE-2026-12151 — undici DoS (unbounded memory), HIGH. Fixed in undici
#   6.27.0 / 7.28.0 / 8.5.0.
#   Affected path: the node:24-alpine base image's BUNDLED npm CLI
#     (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm → node-gyp → undici@6.25.0). NOT an
#     app runtime dependency — the server runs `next start` (node), never the
#     npm CLI / node-gyp, so this undici is unreachable from request-handling
#     code (blast radius = build-time only). Same class as the picomatch
#     exemptions retired in the node:22→24 bump below.
#   Retire when: the node:24-alpine base image refreshes its bundled npm CLI
#     to one whose node-gyp carries undici ≥ 6.27.0 (next Node base-image
#     bump / image rebuild). Re-check with `npm ls undici` in the image.
CVE-2026-12151
#
# Historical note (cleanup-5-node-24-bump, 2026-06-14): the four
# npm-CLI-bundled CVEs that lived here (picomatch DoS / method injection
# CVE-2026-33671 + CVE-2026-33672, brace-expansion DoS CVE-2026-33750,
# ip-address XSS CVE-2026-42338) were all retired by the Node base image
# bump from node:22-alpine → node:24-alpine. The Node 24 image ships an
# npm CLI whose transitive lockfile carries the patched versions of all
# four affected packages. The exemptions are no longer needed.
#
# If a future advisory needs an exemption, include:
#   - the CVE id
#   - the affected package path
#   - WHY the exemption is safe (reachability / blast radius)
#   - the trigger that retires it (specific dep bump, base-image refresh,
#     deprecation of the vulnerable feature)
#
# CVE-2026-9679 (undici DoS, MEDIUM) / CVE-2026-6733 / CVE-2026-11525 (undici,
#   LOW) — same root + blast radius as CVE-2026-12151 above: the affected
#   undici@6.26.0 lives in the node:24-alpine base image's BUNDLED npm CLI
#   (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm → node-gyp → undici), NOT an app runtime
#   dependency. The server runs `next start` (node), never the npm CLI /
#   node-gyp, so this undici is unreachable from request-handling code
#   (blast radius = build-time only). Fixed in undici 6.27.0; npm has not yet
#   bundled a node-gyp carrying it (npm@11.17.0 still ships undici@6.26.0).
#   Retire when: the node:24-alpine base image refreshes its bundled npm CLI
#   to one whose node-gyp carries undici ≥ 6.27.0. Re-check with
#   `npm ls undici` in the image.
CVE-2026-9679
CVE-2026-6733
CVE-2026-11525
#
# CVE-2026-53655 (tar, MEDIUM) — the affected tar@7.5.15 lives in the
#   node:24-alpine base image's BUNDLED npm CLI (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/
#   npm → tar), NOT an app runtime dependency (our own lockfile is pinned to
#   tar ≥ 7.5.16 via the package.json `overrides`). The server never invokes
#   the npm CLI at runtime, so this tar is unreachable (build-time only).
#   Retire when: the node:24-alpine base image refreshes its bundled npm CLI
#   to one carrying tar ≥ 7.5.16. Re-check with `npm ls tar` in the image.
CVE-2026-53655
#
# CVE-2026-14257 (brace-expansion, HIGH) — DoS via a follow-up to the
#   CVE-2026-13149 ReDoS. The affected brace-expansion@5.0.7 lives in the
#   image's GLOBAL npm CLI (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm →
#   brace-expansion; the Dockerfile runs `npm install -g npm@12.0.1`), NOT an
#   app runtime dependency — our own lockfile resolves the top-level
#   brace-expansion to 5.0.8. The server runs `next start` (node), never the
#   npm CLI, so this copy is unreachable from request-handling code (blast
#   radius = build-time only). Same class as the undici / tar npm-CLI-bundled
#   exemptions above, and the earlier brace-expansion CVE-2026-33750 retired
#   in the node:22→24 bump. Fixed in brace-expansion 5.0.8; the newest npm
#   (12.0.1) still bundles 5.0.7.
#   Retire when: the global `npm install -g npm@…` in the Dockerfile moves to
#   an npm whose bundle carries brace-expansion ≥ 5.0.8. Re-check with
#   `npm ls brace-expansion` in the image.
CVE-2026-14257

# ── 2026-08-04 — two NEW advisories against the image's GLOBAL npm CLI ──
#
#   CVE-2026-69152  brace-expansion  5.0.7 → fixed 5.0.9   HIGH
#   CVE-2026-69192  ip-address       10.2.0 → fixed 10.3.1 HIGH
#                   (reached via npm's bundled `socks`)
#
# Same class as CVE-2026-14257 directly above, and the undici / tar
# entries earlier: both live in /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm, the
# GLOBAL CLI installed by `npm install -g npm@12.0.1` (Dockerfile:81) —
# NOT an application runtime dependency. Our own lockfile resolves the
# top-level brace-expansion to 5.0.9 (raised in this same PR) and does
# not carry ip-address at all outside npm's bundle.
#
# The server runs `next start` (node) and never invokes the npm CLI, so
# neither copy is reachable from request-handling code — blast radius is
# build-time only.
#
# npm ships its dependencies BUNDLED, so a package.json `overrides` entry
# cannot rewrite them; the only lever is the npm version itself. Checked
# empirically on 2026-08-04 by unpacking the tarball: npm 12.0.2 (the
# newest release, one ahead of the pinned 12.0.1) STILL bundles
# brace-expansion 5.0.7 and ip-address 10.2.0. There is no npm release to
# move to, which is why this is an ignore rather than a bump.
#
# NOT caused by any change in this PR — both surfaced from a Trivy DB
# refresh; the previous main run (30819169244) scanned the same image
# layer green.
#
# Retire when: an npm release bundles brace-expansion >= 5.0.9 and
# ip-address >= 10.3.1, then move the Dockerfile's `npm install -g npm@…`
# to it and delete these two lines. Re-check with
# `npm view npm version` + unpacking, or `npm ls` inside the image.
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
